{%- comment -%}
  Footer structure:

    1. newsletter band            (sits ABOVE the main structure, not inside
                                   it; feeds the welcome-discount automation)
    2. the giant wordmark (.ftr__moment)
    3. hairline
    4. FOUR NAV COLUMNS, each a Shopify link list (menu_1…menu_4) with its own
       heading — the navigation floor a real shop has
    5. country + language selectors, when the shop actually has more than one
    6. the colophon: registered seller, VAT, both addresses, returns warning,
       email, phone, response note, service hours, right-of-withdrawal link
    7. copyright + Instagram · payment marks (FULL COLOUR) · back to top

  WHY 4 AND 6 CHANGED. The footer used to be a wordmark, three short link
  lists and a nine-line <address> block occupying the fourth column — so the
  widest, most-scrolled-to band in the store was mostly RMA legalese set at
  label size. A shopper reads a footer to answer "is this a real shop and where
  do I go next"; the legalese answers the first question and NOTHING answered
  the second. So: four real navigation columns take the grid, and every legal
  line survives, DEMOTED into the colophon — a single quiet band between the
  columns and the copyright row. Nothing was deleted. It stopped being the
  loudest thing down here.

  Backwards compatible on purpose: menu_1…menu_3 fall back to the old
  menu_shop / menu_help / menu_legal settings, and then to the
  footer-shop / footer-help / footer-legal link lists, so a live store that
  updates the theme files keeps exactly the footer it had.

  Every value is a theme setting — nothing here is hardcoded.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign tel = settings.biz_phone | remove: ' ' | remove: '(' | remove: ')' | remove: '-'

  comment
    Column resolution, written out four times rather than looped: the fallback
    chain differs per column (columns 1-3 carry legacy settings and a
    translated default heading, column 4 is new), and the explicit version is
    the one a merchant-support reader can follow.

    Heading chain: the merchant's own text → the theme's translated heading →
    the link list's own name in Shopify admin. A column never shows an empty
    heading, and a merchant who renames the menu gets that name for free.
  endcomment
  assign m1 = section.settings.menu_1 | default: section.settings.menu_shop | default: linklists['footer-shop']
  assign m2 = section.settings.menu_2 | default: section.settings.menu_help | default: linklists['footer-help']
  assign m3 = section.settings.menu_3 | default: section.settings.menu_legal | default: linklists['footer-legal']
  assign m4 = section.settings.menu_4

  assign h1 = section.settings.menu_1_heading
  if h1 == blank
    assign h1 = 'footer.shop_heading' | t
  endif
  if h1 == blank
    assign h1 = m1.title
  endif

  assign h2 = section.settings.menu_2_heading
  if h2 == blank
    assign h2 = 'footer.help_heading' | t
  endif
  if h2 == blank
    assign h2 = m2.title
  endif

  assign h3 = section.settings.menu_3_heading
  if h3 == blank
    assign h3 = 'footer.legal_heading' | t
  endif
  if h3 == blank
    assign h3 = m3.title
  endif

  assign h4 = section.settings.menu_4_heading
  if h4 == blank
    assign h4 = m4.title
  endif
-%}
<footer class="ftr">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="ftr__nl reveal">
      <h2 class="dl ftr__nl-head">{{ 'footer.newsletter_heading' | t }}</h2>
      <div>
        {%- form 'customer' -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter">
          {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
            <p class="form-status">{{ section.settings.nl_success | escape }}</p>
          {%- else -%}
            {%- if form.errors -%}
              <p class="form-status form-status--error">{{ form.errors | default_errors }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            <div class="ftr__row">
              <label class="visually-hidden" for="ftr-email">{{ 'footer.newsletter.email_label' | t }}</label>
              <input id="ftr-email" type="email" name="contact[email]" placeholder="{{ 'footer.newsletter_placeholder' | t }}" autocomplete="email" required>
              <button type="submit" onclick="document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('theme:newsletter'))">{{ 'footer.newsletter_button' | t }}</button>
            </div>
            <p class="ftr__note lbl-sm mute">{{ 'footer.newsletter_note' | t }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endform -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} The giant wordmark (.ftr__moment). Full page width, ink on
  cream, decorative only — the accessible name lives on the header logo link. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="ftr__moment" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="ftr__wordmark">{%- render 'logo-lockup' -%}</span>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <hr class="rule">

    {%- comment -%} FOUR COLUMNS. Each is a <nav> with its own accessible name:
    four unlabelled lists of links are four unlabelled lists to a screen-reader
    user, and the heading is the only thing that tells them apart. A column
    renders only when its link list exists AND has links — an assigned-but-empty
    menu used to leave a heading standing over nothing. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ftr__cols">
      {%- if m1 != blank and m1.links.size > 0 -%}
        <nav class="ftr__col" aria-label="{{ h1 | escape }}">
          <h2 class="ftr__col-h lbl">{{ h1 | escape }}</h2>
          <ul class="ftr__col-list">
            {%- for link in m1.links -%}
              <li><a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title | escape }}</a></li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </nav>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if m2 != blank and m2.links.size > 0 -%}
        <nav class="ftr__col" aria-label="{{ h2 | escape }}">
          <h2 class="ftr__col-h lbl">{{ h2 | escape }}</h2>
          <ul class="ftr__col-list">
            {%- for link in m2.links -%}
              <li><a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title | escape }}</a></li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </nav>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if m3 != blank and m3.links.size > 0 -%}
        <nav class="ftr__col" aria-label="{{ h3 | escape }}">
          <h2 class="ftr__col-h lbl">{{ h3 | escape }}</h2>
          <ul class="ftr__col-list">
            {%- for link in m3.links -%}
              <li><a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title | escape }}</a></li>
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- comment -%} Cookie handling is covered in the Privacy Policy
            (browser settings) — no separate cookie-settings link needed here. {%- endcomment -%}
          </ul>
        </nav>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if m4 != blank and m4.links.size > 0 -%}
        <nav class="ftr__col" aria-label="{{ h4 | escape }}">
          <h2 class="ftr__col-h lbl">{{ h4 | escape }}</h2>
          <ul class="ftr__col-list">
            {%- for link in m4.links -%}
              <li><a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title | escape }}</a></li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </nav>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Country and language: gives shoppers a way to switch market
    or language manually when the storefront redirects by default. Styled
    <details> panels, never a native <select> (theme rule). Each renders only
    when the shop actually has more than one option — a single-market shop shows
    no control at all rather than a dead one.

    Two separate localization forms, not one: a single form posting both
    country_code and locale_code makes every language button also re-submit the
    country, and a shopper switching language silently loses their market. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if localization.available_countries.size > 1 or localization.available_languages.size > 1 -%}
      <div class="ftr__loc">
        {%- if localization.available_countries.size > 1 -%}
          {%- form 'localization', class: 'ftr-loc__form' -%}
            <details class="ftr-loc">
              <summary class="ftr-loc__current lbl-sm">
                {{ localization.country.name }} ({{ localization.country.currency.iso_code }})
                <span class="acc__sign" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </summary>
              <div class="ftr-loc__panel">
                {%- for country in localization.available_countries -%}
                  <button
                    type="submit"
                    class="ftr-loc__option lbl-sm"
                    name="country_code"
                    value="{{ country.iso_code }}"
                    {% if country.iso_code == localization.country.iso_code %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                  >{{ country.name }} ({{ country.currency.iso_code }})</button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </details>
          {%- endform -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if localization.available_languages.size > 1 -%}
          {%- form 'localization', class: 'ftr-loc__form' -%}
            <details class="ftr-loc">
              <summary class="ftr-loc__current lbl-sm">
                {{ localization.language.endonym_name }}
                <span class="acc__sign" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </summary>
              <div class="ftr-loc__panel">
                {%- for language in localization.available_languages -%}
                  <button
                    type="submit"
                    class="ftr-loc__option lbl-sm"
                    name="locale_code"
                    value="{{ language.iso_code }}"
                    lang="{{ language.iso_code }}"
                    {% if language.iso_code == localization.language.iso_code %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                  >{{ language.endonym_name }}</button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </details>
          {%- endform -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} THE COLOPHON — every legal line the footer used to shout,
    kept in full and set quiet. A GMC reviewer and a first-time shopper both
    look for the registered seller and both addresses in the footer, and the
    Legal Notice page must not be the only place they exist; neither of them
    needs it at the top of the reading order in a column of its own. Nothing
    here was removed when it moved. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ftr__colophon bt">
      <address class="ftr__biz">
        {%- comment %} Every line renders only when its setting is filled. {% endcomment -%}
        {%- if settings.biz_name != blank -%}
          <p>
            <span class="ftr__biz-k">{{ 'footer.business.store_label' | t }}</span> {{ settings.biz_name | escape }}
            {%- if settings.biz_vat != blank -%}<br><span class="ftr__biz-k">{{ 'footer.business.vat_label' | t }}</span> {{ settings.biz_vat | escape }}{%- endif -%}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if settings.biz_address1 != blank -%}
          <p>
            <span class="ftr__biz-k">{{ 'footer.business.company_address_label' | t }}</span><br>
            {{ settings.biz_address1 | escape }}<br>
            {{ settings.biz_city | escape }}, {{ settings.biz_country | escape }}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if settings.biz_wh_line1 != blank -%}
          <p>
            <span class="ftr__biz-k">{{ 'footer.business.warehouse_address_label' | t }}</span><br>
            {{ settings.biz_wh_line1 | escape }}<br>
            {{ settings.biz_wh_line2 | escape }}<br>
            {{ settings.biz_wh_country | escape }}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if settings.biz_returns_note != blank -%}
          <p><span class="ftr__biz-k">{{ 'footer.business.returns_label' | t }}</span> {{ settings.biz_returns_note | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if settings.biz_email != blank or settings.biz_phone != blank -%}
          <p>
            {%- if settings.biz_email != blank -%}
              <span class="ftr__biz-k">{{ 'footer.business.email_label' | t }}</span> <a href="mailto:{{ settings.biz_email }}">{{ settings.biz_email | escape }}</a>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if settings.biz_phone != blank -%}
              {%- if settings.biz_email != blank -%}<br>{%- endif -%}
              <span class="ftr__biz-k">{{ 'footer.business.phone_label' | t }}</span> <a href="tel:{{ tel }}">{{ settings.biz_phone | escape }}</a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.response_note != blank -%}
          <p>{{ section.settings.response_note | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if settings.biz_hours != blank -%}
          <p>
            <span class="ftr__biz-k">{{ 'footer.business.hours_label' | t }}</span><br>
            {{ settings.biz_hours | escape }}<br>
            {{ settings.biz_hours_weekend | escape }}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </address>

      {%- comment -%} The one-line right of withdrawal. Some jurisdictions require
      this link to be more prominent than a buried legal-menu entry, so it keeps
      its own line and its own element rather than becoming the fourteenth item
      in the Legal column. It renders only when a page is picked in the section
      settings. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.withdrawal_page != blank -%}
        <p class="ftr__retractation">
          {{ 'footer.retractation_prompt' | t }}
          <a href="{{ pages[section.settings.withdrawal_page].url }}">{{ 'retractation.trigger' | t }}</a>
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="ftr__bottom lbl-sm mute bt">
      <span class="ftr__copy">
        &copy; {{ 'now' | date: '%Y' }} {{ shop.name }}. {{ 'footer.copyright.rights' | t }}
        {%- if section.settings.social_instagram != blank -%}
          <a class="ftr__social" href="{{ section.settings.social_instagram }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{ shop.name | escape }} on Instagram">
            {% render 'icon', name: 'instagram', size: 18 %}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
      {%- comment -%} Payment marks in FULL COLOUR, straight from the shop's own
      enabled gateways — `payment_type_svg_tag` is the only source that can never
      advertise a method the store does not actually accept. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if shop.enabled_payment_types.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="ftr__pay" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'general.accepted_payment_methods' | t }}">
          {%- for type in shop.enabled_payment_types -%}
            {{ type | payment_type_svg_tag }}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      <a class="ftr__top tlink" href="#main">{{ 'footer.back_to_top' | t }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Footer",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Newsletter" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "nl_success", "label": "Success message", "default": "You're on the list. New pieces land in your inbox first." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Navigation columns" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Four columns of links. Leave a heading empty to use the theme's own wording, or the menu's name. A column with no menu is hidden." },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_1", "label": "Column 1 menu" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "menu_1_heading", "label": "Column 1 heading", "info": "Empty = \"Shop\"." },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_2", "label": "Column 2 menu" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "menu_2_heading", "label": "Column 2 heading", "info": "Empty = \"Help\"." },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_3", "label": "Column 3 menu" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "menu_3_heading", "label": "Column 3 heading", "info": "Empty = \"Legal\"." },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_4", "label": "Column 4 menu" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "menu_4_heading", "label": "Column 4 heading", "info": "Empty = the menu's own name." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Link lists (legacy)" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Kept so existing stores are not reset. Column 1–3 above take priority when set; these are used when they are empty." },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_shop", "label": "Shop menu" },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_help", "label": "Help menu" },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_legal", "label": "Legal menu" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Business information" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "response_note", "label": "Response-time note", "default": "We aim to respond within 24–48 hours.", "info": "Everything else in this block comes from Theme settings → Business. It sits in the quiet colophon band under the columns." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "social_instagram", "label": "Instagram URL (empty = hidden)" },
    { "type": "page", "id": "withdrawal_page", "label": "Right-of-withdrawal page (optional)", "info": "When set, a one-line withdrawal link renders in the colophon." }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
